  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_section_1",
      "section_title": "Bag-valve-mask (Ambu bag)",
      "section_order": 1,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_1",
          "subsection_title": "Bag-Valve-Mask (BVM / Ambu Bag)",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_1",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The bag-valve-mask (BVM) is a handheld device used to provide positive-pressure ventilation to patients who are not breathing adequately or have stopped breathing. It is a high-yield OSCE instrument because examiners commonly assess identification, components, assembly, mask seal, ventilation technique, complications, and differences between adult, pediatric, and neonatal resuscitation."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "Identification and definition",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_2",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Name: Bag-valve-mask resuscitator, commonly called an Ambu bag."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Definition: A manual ventilation device consisting of a self-inflating or flow-inflating bag, a one-way valve, and a face mask. When the bag is squeezed, air or an oxygen-enriched gas mixture is delivered into the patient's lungs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Key principle: Positive-pressure ventilation — air is pushed into the lungs rather than being drawn in by normal inspiratory effort."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "Types of resuscitators",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_3",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "A. Self-inflating bag"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The bag refills automatically after being squeezed. It can provide ventilation even without a compressed-gas source, although supplemental oxygen and a reservoir are needed for a high inspired oxygen concentration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "B. Flow-inflating bag"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires a gas supply and appropriate technique to inflate. It is more commonly associated with anaesthesia and specialist neonatal settings."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "C. T-piece resuscitator"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A related neonatal ventilation device that can deliver controlled pressure when correctly set up. It is not a conventional bag-valve-mask device."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "Components and their functions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "1. Ventilation bag"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The squeezable chamber that delivers gas to the patient."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Face mask"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Fits over the nose and mouth to create a seal. The correct size should cover both without pressing excessively on the eyes."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Patient valve"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Directs gas toward the patient during bag compression and allows exhaled gas to leave through the appropriate expiratory pathway."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "4. Oxygen tubing and reservoir"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Connect the device to an oxygen source and reservoir when available to increase the oxygen concentration delivered."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "5. Pressure-relief valve, if fitted"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Limits excessive pressure in some models. Its presence does not eliminate the risk of excessive ventilation pressure."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "Indications and uses",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The BVM is indicated when a patient requires assisted ventilation, including:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Apnoea or respiratory arrest."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ineffective breathing with inadequate ventilation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Respiratory failure with exhaustion or deteriorating consciousness."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ventilation during cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Preoxygenation or assisted ventilation before advanced airway management."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Neonatal resuscitation when positive-pressure ventilation is indicated, using an appropriate neonatal device and protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important distinction: Supplemental oxygen alone may not correct apnoea. A patient who is not ventilating adequately needs ventilation as well as oxygen, as clinically indicated."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Rapid and portable: Can be used at the bedside, in the emergency department, in ambulances, and during resuscitation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Does not require electricity: A self-inflating bag can work without a powered ventilator."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Provides positive-pressure ventilation: Useful when spontaneous breathing is absent or inadequate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can deliver high oxygen concentrations: When correctly connected to an oxygen source and reservoir."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Available in multiple sizes: Adult, child, infant, and neonatal models are available."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can be used with airway adjuncts: Such as an oropharyngeal airway or nasopharyngeal airway when appropriate."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "Disadvantages and limitations",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Maintaining a good mask seal can be difficult, especially with facial hair, facial trauma, or unusual facial anatomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "One-person ventilation may be ineffective in patients with poor mask fit or airway obstruction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Excessive ventilation may cause gastric inflation, regurgitation, aspiration, or lung injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It requires training and repeated practice."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It may be less effective than ventilation through a secured advanced airway in some circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Without supplemental oxygen, the device generally delivers air rather than a high oxygen concentration."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "How to assemble and use the BVM",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This is a common practical OSCE station."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Demonstrate the steps on a manikin during an examination."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_9",
              "group_title": "Step 1 — Prepare the equipment",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Perform hand hygiene and use appropriate PPE."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check that the bag, valve, mask, oxygen tubing, and reservoir are intact."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Select the correct mask and bag size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Connect oxygen and the reservoir if available; set the flow according to the device manufacturer's instructions."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check that the bag refills and the valves function correctly."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_10",
              "group_title": "Step 2 — Assess the patient",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check responsiveness and assess breathing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Activate the emergency response system and obtain resuscitation equipment as appropriate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If the patient is unresponsive and not breathing normally, assess for cardiac arrest and follow the relevant BLS/CPR algorithm."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not delay lifesaving ventilation while waiting for supplemental oxygen or advanced equipment."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_11",
              "group_title": "Step 3 — Position the airway",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_11.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_12.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If there is no suspicion of cervical spine injury, use the head-tilt–chin-lift manoeuvre."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If cervical spine injury is suspected, use a jaw thrust while maintaining spinal precautions; airway opening and oxygenation take priority if these manoeuvres are insufficient."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Remove only visible airway obstructions and suction secretions or vomit when indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Consider an appropriate airway adjunct if the patient has no gag reflex and there is no contraindication."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_12",
              "group_title": "Step 4 — Apply the mask and obtain a seal",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_13.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_14.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_15.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "One-person technique"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Place the mask over the bridge of the nose and mouth, extending to the chin."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use the thumb and index finger to secure the mask."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use the remaining fingers to lift the jaw toward the mask."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Avoid pressing into the soft tissues beneath the chin, which may obstruct the airway."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Squeeze the bag while maintaining the seal."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Two-person technique — often preferred"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Person 1: Uses both hands to maintain the mask seal and lift the jaw."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Person 2: Squeezes the bag slowly, delivering the breath over approximately one second."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The two-person method is particularly useful when the mask seal is difficult to maintain."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_13",
              "group_title": "Step 5 — Deliver ventilation",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Squeeze the bag smoothly, delivering only enough gas to produce visible chest rise."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allow the chest to fall before delivering the next breath."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Observe chest movement and assess whether ventilation is effective."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Avoid rapid or forceful squeezing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If the chest does not rise, reassess the mask seal, airway position, obstruction, and equipment."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_14",
              "group_title": "Step 6 — Reassess",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Look for:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Visible chest rise and fall."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Improving oxygen saturation, where measurable."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Improvement in colour and clinical condition."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Evidence of effective ventilation, including appropriate exhalation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If ventilation remains ineffective, call for help, optimise the airway and seal, consider an adjunct, and follow the relevant resuscitation algorithm."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "Ventilation rates: adult, child, infant and neonate",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_15",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "These rates apply to different clinical situations. Do not use one rate for every patient. Follow the current local resuscitation protocol and the patient's clinical circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Situation",
                    "Typical ventilation approach"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Adult with a pulse but inadequate breathing",
                      "1 breath every 6 seconds (about 10/min)"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Child or infant with a pulse but inadequate breathing",
                      "1 breath every 2–3 seconds (about 20–30/min), following the applicable pediatric BLS guideline"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Adult CPR without an advanced airway",
                      "30 compressions : 2 breaths"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Child/infant CPR without an advanced airway",
                      "30:2 for a single rescuer; 15:2 for two trained rescuers under the applicable pediatric BLS algorithm"
                    ],
                    [
                      "CPR with an advanced airway",
                      "Continuous compressions with protocol-directed asynchronous ventilation; typical adult rate is 1 breath every 6 seconds"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Newborn resuscitation at birth",
                      "Usually 40–60 ventilation breaths/min when positive-pressure ventilation is indicated, following neonatal resuscitation guidance"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE safety point: Each breath should generally be delivered over about one second, with enough volume to produce visible chest rise. Excessive volume or rate can be harmful."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "Contraindications and precautions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_16",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "There is no absolute contraindication to lifesaving BVM ventilation when a patient needs it. However, certain situations make ventilation more difficult or increase risk."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_17",
              "group_title": "Important precautions",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Suspected cervical spine injury: Use appropriate spinal precautions while ensuring the airway is open."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Facial trauma or deformity: A reliable mask seal may be difficult; seek alternative airway strategies and expert help."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Vomiting or heavy secretions: Suction as needed and minimise aspiration risk."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Upper airway obstruction: Correct positioning and manage the obstruction; bag squeezing alone may not overcome a blocked airway."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Risk of gastric inflation: Use gentle breaths and avoid excessive pressure or rate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Possible foreign body: Follow the appropriate choking/airway-obstruction algorithm."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_18",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Cause or prevention"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Gastric inflation",
                      "Excessive pressure, excessive volume, or rapid ventilation"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Regurgitation and aspiration",
                      "Gastric inflation or vomiting, particularly in patients with reduced airway reflexes"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Barotrauma",
                      "Excessive airway pressure causing lung injury"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Hypoventilation",
                      "Poor mask seal, obstruction, inadequate ventilation, or equipment malfunction"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Hyperventilation",
                      "Ventilating too rapidly or delivering excessive volumes"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Eye injury",
                      "Mask pressure applied over the eyes"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Delayed definitive care",
                      "Prolonged attempts at mask ventilation without escalation when ineffective"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "Pediatric and neonatal considerations",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_19",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_16.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_17.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_18.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use an appropriately sized pediatric or neonatal mask and ventilation device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The mask should cover the nose and mouth without covering the eyes or extending excessively beyond the chin."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Infants and children have smaller airways, so positioning and airway patency are particularly important."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Deliver gentle breaths sufficient for visible chest rise; avoid adult-sized volumes."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Neonatal resuscitation at birth follows a specific algorithm, including specialised equipment, ventilation assessment, and escalation when indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In newborns, effective lung inflation is a critical priority when positive-pressure ventilation is required."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "Memory aid: BAG MASK",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_20",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "B"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Breathing: Assess breathing and recognise the need for support."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "A"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Airway: Open the airway and remove visible obstruction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "G"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Gear: Check the bag, valve, mask, and oxygen connection."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "M"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Mask: Apply the correct size and maintain a seal."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "A"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Air entry: Squeeze gently and look for chest rise."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "S"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "See: Observe chest movement and clinical response."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "K"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Keep reassessing: Correct leaks, obstruction, or inadequate ventilation."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "Common OSCE examiner questions and model answers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_21",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is the main function of a BVM?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "To provide positive-pressure ventilation when spontaneous breathing is absent or inadequate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. Why is a good mask seal important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It prevents air leakage and helps deliver sufficient ventilation to the lungs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. How do you know ventilation is effective?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Visible chest rise, chest fall during expiration, and improvement in the patient's clinical condition. Oxygen saturation can support assessment but should not be the sole indicator."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What would you do if the chest does not rise?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reposition the airway, correct the mask seal, check the equipment, suction secretions if indicated, consider an airway adjunct, and seek help if ventilation remains ineffective."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Why is a two-person technique often better?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "One rescuer can maintain the airway and mask seal using both hands while the other delivers controlled breaths."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What are the major complications?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Gastric inflation, aspiration, barotrauma, ineffective ventilation, and hyperventilation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Can a self-inflating BVM work without oxygen?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Yes. It can deliver room air, but supplemental oxygen with an appropriate reservoir is needed to deliver a higher oxygen concentration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What is the difference between oxygen therapy and BVM ventilation?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Oxygen therapy increases the oxygen concentration available for the patient to breathe. BVM ventilation actively moves gas into the lungs when the patient cannot ventilate adequately."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_15",
          "subsection_title": "Common mistakes that lose OSCE marks",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_22",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Failing to check the equipment before use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selecting the wrong mask size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Placing the mask over the eyes or failing to cover the chin properly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Pressing on the soft tissues beneath the chin instead of lifting the jaw."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Squeezing the bag too forcefully or too rapidly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Failing to observe chest rise."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ignoring persistent obstruction or mask leakage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Forgetting to reassess the patient and request help when ventilation is ineffective."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_16",
          "subsection_title": "Mini OSCE station",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_23",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Scenario: A 54-year-old man is found unresponsive and is not breathing normally. You are asked to demonstrate ventilation using a bag-valve-mask on a manikin."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Expected approach:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ensure safety, assess responsiveness and breathing, and activate the emergency response."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Recognise possible cardiac arrest and follow the appropriate CPR algorithm."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prepare and check the BVM, selecting an appropriate mask."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Open the airway, using the appropriate manoeuvre for the circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Obtain a firm mask seal; use a two-person technique if available."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Deliver breaths sufficient for visible chest rise, following the applicable resuscitation algorithm."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reassess ventilation effectiveness and continue CPR or other indicated care without unnecessary delays."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Examiner's key point: The candidate should demonstrate effective ventilation, not merely squeeze the bag."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_subsection_17",
          "subsection_title": "Quick revision checklist",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bag_valve_mask_ambu_bag_group_24",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can you perform this station?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "0/8",
                    "Identify the BVM and explain its principle",
                    "Name the bag, mask, valve, oxygen tubing and reservoir",
                    "Explain indications and limitations",
                    "Demonstrate airway positioning",
                    "Demonstrate a one-person mask seal",
                    "Explain the two-person technique",
                    "State the appropriate ventilation rate for the scenario",
                    "Identify complications and correct ineffective ventilation"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}